          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ঘিনঘিনে (ghinghine) doubles ghin, \"loathing\", which CDIAL lists for Bengali under Sanskrit ghṛṇā (CDIAL 4500), and adds the adjective ending -e."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
