          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "বিতৃষ্ণা — bitrishnā — \"aversion; distaste\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "রোজ একই খাবার খেয়ে অরুণের বিতৃষ্ণা এল। roj eki khābār kheye ôruner bitrishnā elô. Eating the same food every day, Arun grew sick of it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "বিতৃষ্ণা (bitrishnā) is a tatsama, Sanskrit vitṛṣṇā, which Monier-Williams gives as freedom from desire, vi- \"without\" on tṛṣṇā \"thirst\"; Bengali has pushed it on to distaste, a sense the dictionary does not give."
            }
          ]
        },
